cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PhantomTap: ML-Guided RFID/NFC Fuzzing & Access-Control Auditing"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Choksi"
    given-names: "Krishita Sanjay"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Krishita17/PhantomTap"
abstract: >-
  PhantomTap turns a Flipper Zero into an intelligent access-control auditing
  platform. A host-side layer learns the structure of observed credentials,
  generates the next-best test credential via active learning instead of blind
  brute force, and produces an explainable, prioritized access-control risk
  report. Deliberately a defensive auditing tool: all experiments use synthetic
  credential populations or the author's own cards and readers.
keywords:
  - RFID
  - NFC
  - Flipper Zero
  - access control
  - security audit
  - Wiegand
  - MIFARE
  - active learning
  - physical security
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-15"
